<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 2.48 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 2.48 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.1420 to the dollar, down from 3.1350 on Tuesday, and at 1.8330 to the mark, up from 1.8360, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 2.48 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, and 2.50 percent from the floating rate against than Tuesday's 2.44 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
